speechtext:
Order. I would suggest to the hon. member for Quebec West that this is another case of an interjection because he did not agree with something said by the hon. member who technically has the floor. If the hon. member for Quebec West feels his remarks were misinterpreted or that

Northern Ontario Pipe Line Corporation for good reasons he should interrupt, I will assure him he will have an opportunity to make corrections-not necessarily to make another speech-at the conclusion of the remarks of the hon. member for St. Mary. The point raised by the hon. member for Quebec West is one of debate and not one of order.
